  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Chemicals risk management  in Serbia 2016-2022 - Chemicals risk management in Serbia, 2016-2022</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Kemikaliesamarbete med Serbien 2016-2022</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Cooperation on chemicals risk management supporting Serbia&apos;s preparations for EU accession, including harmonisation of regulations, capacity building, especially on biocides, improved chemicals registry and communication. The project started in 2016, has been extended to 2022.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Insatsen &#xe4;r en forts&#xe4;ttning p&#xe5; ett l&#xe5;ngvarigt svenskt samarbete inom kemikalieomr&#xe5;det. Projektet som startade 2016 f&#xf6;rl&#xe4;ngdes 2020 till att fortg&#xe5; till 2022.  Det svenska st&#xf6;det fokuserar p&#xe5; att fortsatt kompetensutveckling och harmonisering av nationell lagstiftning med EUs regelverk. Samarbetet inneh&#xe5;ller ocks&#xe5; st&#xf6;d till en uppgradering av det nationella kemikalieregistret, inkluderar IT-utveckling, samt ett brett arbete f&#xf6;r institutionell utveckling f&#xf6;r att klara av kommande EU-krav. Genom f&#xf6;rl&#xe4;ngningen ges ett &#xf6;kat fokus till kommunikation till allm&#xe4;nheten.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall objective of the project was to strengthen Serbia&#xb4;s preparation&#xa0;for EU chemical and biocidal legislation and management, which&#xa0;will improve movement of goods and chemical safety and health in Serbia and the EU. The project developed IT solutions, built administrative capacities, prepared appropriate legislation, and strengthened communication on EU chemical legislation. The project was implemented by the Swedish Chemicals Agency, KemI, together with the&#xa0;Department for Chemical&#xa0;Management at the&#xa0;Serbian Ministry for Environmental Protection. The project, started in 2016,&#xa0;and was finalized in 2022. The total time of cooperation between KemI and the Serbian Ministry of Environmental Protection was 13 years.</narrative>
  </description>
